Not all replication events can be applied in parallel. What if the binary log
contains two statements updating the same row?
update limbs set arms=8 where thing='squid';
update limbs set arms=10 where thing='squid';
Depending on the order of events, the limbs table will have either 8 or 10
arms for the squid. If these two statements are executed in different order on
the source and replica, they will end up with different data.
